  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The offense left runners everywhere and scored just once. That loss sits heavier than the margin suggests.",
    "what_this_means": "Cesar Perdomo pitched well enough to win. Five and a third innings, two runs, no disasters. But the Giants wasted the one clean chance they created. In the fourth, they pushed two across and briefly led. Then Minnesota answered in the seventh, and the Giants went silent. They had six runners in scoring position and converted one. Five hits. Seven strikeouts. The bullpen stayed clean but couldn't fix what the bats broke early. This is the pattern tightening: good pitching, sparse hitting, and narrow windows closing before they open again.",
    "what_to_watch": "LAD arrives tomorrow night with another test waiting. Yunior Marte takes the mound against a Dodgers lineup that doesn't miss mistakes, so precision matters more than power. Exactly what this team has struggled to deliver when it counts most.",
